      "problem": "Solve for $q$ where $\\frac{3-2q}{3}=-\\frac{1}{5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We transfer the negative into the numerator of the fraction, and proceed with cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3-2q}{3} & =-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ (3-2q)\\cdot 5 & =3\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-2q)\\cdot 5 & =3\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 15-10q & =-3 \\\\ 15-10q-15 & =-3-15 \\\\ -10q & =-18 \\\\ \\frac{-10q}{-10} & =\\frac{-18}{-10} \\\\ q & =\\frac{18}{10} \\\\ q & =\\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
